  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is clearly the superior RNA encoder (0.520 rna_only vs 0.435 multimodal with scgpt), weighted fusion slightly edges out concat (0.537 vs 0.532), and the image modality adds a small but real benefit over RNA-only (~1.2%). However, we have only tested imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder. Uncertainty: it is unknown whether resnet50 would match, exceed, or underperform imagenet_vit_l in the multimodal setting, and this choice will affect the final configuration. Question: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, weighted fusion) is a clean single-variable swap of the image encoder relative to our best result (config_051, same but imagenet_vit_l). This isolates the image-encoder effect while holding the RNA encoder, profile setting, and fusion strategy at their best-supported values. Rationale: Under a tight budget, this is the highest-information next step because it (a) builds on our strongest evidence, (b) changes only one variable to cleanly attribute any performance shift to the image encoder, and (c) directly informs whether we should invest remaining budget in resnet50-based or ViT-based multimodal pipelines for subsequent multiprofile/aggregation experiments."
}

